 ```
 
+## Build on macOS (Apple Silicon or Intel)
+
+The Python extension builds from source with Apple clang 17 or newer, without Bazel:
+
+```bash
+python3 -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
+pip install "pybind11==2.12.0" setuptools wheel numpy
+pip install ./kickmix
+PYTHONPATH=kickmix pytest kickmix/src
+```
+
+On Apple Silicon the `b128`/`b256` word types use NEON (`simd/b128_neon.h`,
+`simd/b256_neon.h`); `b512` falls back to the portable implementation. Bazel
+targets (`bazel test kickmix:kickmix_test`, `bazel run kickmix:kickmix_perf`)
+also work on macOS with `bazelisk` installed from Homebrew.
+
 ## Build Portable Python Wheel (with cibuildwheel)
 
 ```bash
